nd":"identifier","text":"clusteringCoefficient"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficient(of:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"clusteringCoefficient(of:)"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least 